## std/json.pengu — strict JSON (RFC 8259): parser, serializer, DOM and JSON Pointer.
##
## `std.json` is the complete JSON implementation for PenguScript: a strict
## recursive-descent parser with byte-exact error positions, a serializer whose
## float output round-trips, a DOM (`JsonValue`) that preserves object insertion
## order, JSON Pointer (RFC 6901), recursive key search, deep merge, validation
## without building a DOM, an arena mode for one-shot payloads, and a practical
## JSON Schema subset.
##
## It covers everything Python's `json` module does, and adds:
## JSON Pointer, `find_key`, `validate` (no DOM), `deep_merge`, `parse_in_arena`
## and `validate_schema`. The only deliberate difference is ownership: every
## value is explicitly owned, and every query that hands out a subtree returns a
## deep copy the caller can `banish`. There is no hidden GC.
##
## ## Example: parse, query, free
## ```pengu
## import std.json
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var parsed as result of JsonValue to JsonError is calling json.parse with "{\"name\":\"pengu\",\"tags\":[1,2]}"
##     var root as JsonValue is parsed or:
##         calling spark.panic with error.message
##         return 1
##     defer banish root
##
##     var name as maybe JsonValue is calling root.get with "name"
##     var n as JsonValue is name or:
##         return 1
##     defer banish n
##     var text as string is (calling n.as_string) or else ""
##     calling spark.println with text                       # pengu
##
##     var second as JsonValue is (calling root.pointer with "/tags/1") or:
##         return 1
##     defer banish second
##     calling spark.println with "{(calling second.as_int) or else 0}"   # 2
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Ownership (read this once)
## - `parse` and `parse_in_arena` return a `JsonValue` that owns every string,
##   list and entry below it. `banish root` releases the whole tree (derived
##   `Nexus` recurses through `list of JsonValue` and `list of JsonEntry`).
## - A query that returns a `JsonValue` (`at`, `get`, `first`, `last`,
##   `pointer`, `find_key`, `clone`) returns a **deep copy**. It is independent
##   of the source value and must be banished.
## - `as_string` returns an owned copy; `as_array`, `as_object`, `values` and
##   `entries` return owned deep copies. Release a `list of JsonValue` with
##   `free_values`, a `list of JsonEntry` with `free_entries`, and a
##   `list of string` with `free_strings` (their `banish` only frees the list
##   buffer, exactly like every other PenguScript list).
## - The `maybe` wrapper around those results is released by `banish`; use the
##   `or:` / `or else` forms to move the payload out and free the box in one
##   step.
## - `parse_in_arena` returns a value whose strings and list buffers live in the
##   arena. `banish arena` releases everything at once, and banishing the
##   returned value is a safe no-op. Do not mutate an arena-backed value: its
##   lists are immutable (`cap < 0` marks them).
## - `stringify` returns an owned string.
##
## ## Complexity
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `parse`, `validate` | O(n) time, O(depth) stack |
## | `stringify` | O(size of the value) |
## | `pointer` | O(path tokens × object size) |
## | `find_key` | O(size of the tree) |
## | `deep_merge` | O(size of both trees) |
## | `clone` | O(size of the subtree) |
## | `array_len`, `object_len`, `is_*` | O(1) |
## | `has_key`, `get`, `at` | O(object/array size) |
##
## ## Errors
## Every parser diagnostic carries `kind`, `message`, a 1-indexed `line` and
## `col`, and the absolute `offset` in bytes. `JsonError.format` renders the
## canonical `line:col: message` form.
##
## ## Divergences from Python `json`
## - Integers are `i64`. A literal outside the `i64` range is `IntegerOverflow`,
##   not a big integer (PenguScript is zero-cost and has no bigints).
## - `parse` rejects `NaN`/`Infinity`, comments and trailing commas by default;
##   `ParseOptions` opts in. Python always rejects NaN output unless
##   `allow_nan=True`; so does this module.
## - Duplicate object keys: the last value wins, at the position of the first
##   occurrence (Python keeps the first insertion position too).
## - Floats are printed with the shortest round-tripping representation, then
##   formatted like Python (`1.0`, `10000000000.0`, `1e+20`, `1e-05`).
##
## ## Runtime note
## List headers with `cap < 0` are non-owning views over arena memory. The
## runtime treats their `data` pointer as borrowed, so `banish` is a no-op and
## `push` refuses to grow them. `std.json` is the only producer today.

import std.arena
import std.builder
import std.spark

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## JSON module version.
const JSON_VERSION as string is "2.12.0"

## Default maximum nesting depth accepted by `parse` (matches CPython's default
## recursion limit).
const JSON_MAX_DEPTH as int is 1000

## The byte value of `\n`, used by the line/column tracker.
const JSON_NEWLINE as int is 10

## The byte value of `\r`.
const JSON_CARRIAGE_RETURN as int is 13

## The byte value of `"`.
const JSON_QUOTE as int is 34

## The byte value of `\`.
const JSON_BACKSLASH as int is 92

## The byte value of `/`.
const JSON_SLASH as int is 47

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error model
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## What went wrong while parsing or validating JSON.
omen JsonErrorKind:
    ## The input ended before a complete value was read.
    UnexpectedEof
    ## A byte cannot start the construct the parser expected.
    UnexpectedChar
    ## A number is malformed (`01`, `1.`, `1e`, ...) or out of range.
    InvalidNumber
    ## A string is unterminated or contains a raw control byte.
    InvalidString
    ## A `\` escape is not one of the ten RFC 8259 escapes.
    InvalidEscape
    ## A `\uXXXX` escape is malformed, a surrogate is unpaired, or the
    ## codepoint is above `U+10FFFF`.
    InvalidUnicode
    ## A bare literal (`null`, `true`, `false`) was misspelled.
    InvalidLiteral
    ## A complete value is followed by non-whitespace bytes.
    TrailingCharacters
    ## Nesting exceeded `ParseOptions.max_depth`.
    DepthExceeded
    ## An integer literal does not fit in `i64`.
    IntegerOverflow
    ## The source is not valid UTF-8.
    InvalidUtf8

## A parser or validation failure.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns `message`; `banish err` releases it (derived `Nexus`).
rune JsonError derive Nexus, Par:
    ## The failure category.
    kind as JsonErrorKind
    ## A human-readable explanation, without the position prefix.
    message as string
    ## 1-indexed line of the failure.
    line as int
    ## 1-indexed byte column of the failure.
    col as int
    ## 0-indexed absolute byte offset of the failure.
    offset as int

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOM
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## A JSON value.
##
## The model is algebraic because each variant carries a different payload. It
## preserves object insertion order (`list of JsonEntry`, not a `map`), so
## `stringify` reproduces the document's member order unless `sort_keys` asks
## for alphabetical order.
##
## ## Variantes
## - `Null`: the literal `null`.
## - `Bool`: `true` or `false`.
## - `Int`: an integral number that fits `i64`.
## - `Float`: a number with a fraction or exponent, as `f64`.
## - `Str`: an unescaped UTF-8 string.
## - `Arr`: an array, in document order.
## - `Obj`: an object, in insertion order.
##
## ## Memoria
## A `JsonValue` owns every string and list below it. `banish v` releases the
## whole tree because the derived `Nexus` recurses through the two lists.
omen JsonValue derive Nexus, Par, Imago:
    ## The JSON `null`.
    Null
    ## A boolean.
    Bool with value as bool
    ## An integer (`i64`).
    Int with value as i64
    ## An IEEE-754 double.
    Float with value as f64
    ## A string.
    Str with value as string
    ## An array.
    Arr with items as list of JsonValue
    ## An object.
    Obj with entries as list of JsonEntry

## One member of a JSON object, in insertion order.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns `key` and `value`; `banish entry` releases both.
rune JsonEntry derive Nexus, Par, Imago:
    ## The member name, unescaped and decoded.
    key as string
    ## The member value.
    value as JsonValue

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parse and serialize options
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Knobs for `parse_with`, `validate` and `parse_in_arena`.
rune ParseOptions derive Par:
    ## Accept `NaN`, `Infinity` and `-Infinity` (default `false`).
    allow_non_standard as bool
    ## Maximum nesting depth (default `1000`).
    max_depth as int
    ## Accept `//` and `/* */` comments (default `false`).
    allow_comments as bool
    ## Accept a trailing comma before `]` or `}` (default `false`).
    allow_trailing_commas as bool
    ## Reject raw control bytes inside strings when `true` (default `true`).
    ## When `false`, bytes below `0x20` are accepted verbatim, like Python's
    ## `strict=False`.
    strict as bool

## The strict RFC 8259 defaults.
##
## ## Retorno
## `{allow_non_standard: false, max_depth: 1000, allow_comments: false,
## allow_trailing_commas: false, strict: true}`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var opts as json.ParseOptions is calling json.default_parse_options
## ```
weave default_parse_options into ParseOptions:
    return with allow_non_standard is false, max_depth is JSON_MAX_DEPTH, allow_comments is false, allow_trailing_commas is false, strict is true

## Knobs for `stringify_with` and `write_to_builder`.
rune SerializeOptions derive Par:
    ## Spaces per nesting level; `0` (default) emits compact JSON.
    indent as int
    ## Sort object keys with a byte-wise comparison (default `false`).
    sort_keys as bool
    ## Escape every non-ASCII codepoint as `\uXXXX` (default `false`).
    ensure_ascii as bool
    ## Escape `/` as `\/` (default `false`).
    escape_slash as bool
    ## Emit `NaN`/`Infinity`/`-Infinity` instead of panicking (default `false`).
    allow_nan as bool
    ## With `indent == 0`, use `,`/`:` (default `true`) instead of `, `/`: `.
    compact_separators as bool
    ## Append a final `\n` (default `false`).
    trailing_newline as bool

## The default serializer settings: compact, insertion order, UTF-8 direct.
##
## ## Retorno
## `{indent: 0, sort_keys: false, ensure_ascii: false, escape_slash: false,
## allow_nan: false, compact_separators: true, trailing_newline: false}`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var opts as json.SerializeOptions is calling json.default_serialize_options
## ```
weave default_serialize_options into SerializeOptions:
    return with indent is 0, sort_keys is false, ensure_ascii is false, escape_slash is false, allow_nan is false, compact_separators is true, trailing_newline is false

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private C bridges
#
# Every helper states why it exists and what it owns. They are module-private.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Returns `-1` when `s` is valid UTF-8, else the byte offset of the first
## offending sequence.
##
## ## Motivo
## The parser validates the whole source once, up front, so `parse_string` can
## copy multibyte sequences byte by byte without re-decoding them.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
antiquus _json_valid_utf8 with s as string into int:
    r"""
const unsigned char *p = (const unsigned char *)(s.data ? s.data : "");
int i = 0;
while (i < s.len) {
    unsigned c = p[i];
    if (c < 0x80u) { i++; continue; }
    int len; unsigned cp;
    if ((c & 0xE0u) == 0xC0u) { len = 2; cp = c & 0x1Fu; }
    else if ((c & 0xF0u) == 0xE0u) { len = 3; cp = c & 0x0Fu; }
    else if ((c & 0xF8u) == 0xF0u) { len = 4; cp = c & 0x07u; }
    else { return i; }
    if (i + len > s.len) { return i; }
    for (int k = 1; k < len; k++) {
        unsigned cc = p[i + k];
        if ((cc & 0xC0u) != 0x80u) { return i + k; }
        cp = (cp << 6) | (cc & 0x3Fu);
    }
    if (len == 2 && cp < 0x80u) { return i; }
    if (len == 3 && cp < 0x800u) { return i; }
    if (len == 4 && cp < 0x10000u) { return i; }
    if (cp > 0x10FFFFu) { return i; }
    if (cp >= 0xD800u && cp <= 0xDFFFu) { return i; }
    i += len;
}
return -1;
"""

## Parses the exact byte range `[start, end)` of `s` as a base-10 `i64`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `strtoll` detects `ERANGE` for both ends of the `i64` range, which the
## parser cannot do with an accumulator without special-casing `i64` min.
##
## ## Memoria
## Writes `out`; allocates nothing.
antiquus _json_strtoll with s as string, start as int, end as int, out as ref to i64 into bool:
    r"""
if (start < 0 || end < start || end > s.len) return false;
char *endp = NULL;
errno = 0;
long long v = strtoll(s.data + start, &endp, 10);
if (errno == ERANGE || endp != s.data + end) return false;
*out = (int64_t)v;
return true;
"""

## Parses the exact byte range `[start, end)` of `s` as an `f64`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `strtod` is the correctly-rounded decimal-to-binary conversion; the result
## must round-trip through `stringify`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Writes `out`; allocates nothing.
antiquus _json_strtod with s as string, start as int, end as int, out as ref to f64 into bool:
    r"""
if (start < 0 || end < start || end > s.len) return false;
char *endp = NULL;
errno = 0;
double v = strtod(s.data + start, &endp);
if (endp != s.data + end) return false;
if (errno == ERANGE && (v == 0.0 || v == HUGE_VAL || v == -HUGE_VAL)) return false;
*out = (double)v;
return true;
"""

## Formats an `f64` with the shortest representation that round-trips, in the
## same style as Python's `repr`: fixed notation for decimal exponents in
## `[-4, 16)`, scientific otherwise, always with a decimal part for integral
## values (`1.0`, `10000000000.0`).
##
## ## Motivo
## `snprintf("%g")` truncates to six significant digits, and `%.17g` is not the
## shortest form. The loop over precisions finds the minimal `p` for which
## `strtod` returns the original bit pattern, then rewrites it in the Python
## layout.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned string; release it with `banish`.
antiquus _json_format_f64 with f as f64 into string:
    r"""
char buf[64];
if (isnan(f)) return pengu_string_new("NaN");
if (isinf(f)) return f < 0 ? pengu_string_new("-Infinity") : pengu_string_new("Infinity");
if (f == 0.0) {
    return signbit(f) ? pengu_string_new("-0.0") : pengu_string_new("0.0");
}
int p;
for (p = 1; p <= 17; p++) {
    snprintf(buf, sizeof buf, "%.*g", p, f);
    if (strtod(buf, NULL) == f) break;
}
if (p > 17) p = 17;
snprintf(buf, sizeof buf, "%.*e", p - 1, f);
const char *q = buf;
char sign = 0;
if (*q == '-') { sign = '-'; q++; }
char digits[32];
int nd = 0;
while (*q && *q != 'e' && *q != 'E') {
    if (*q >= '0' && *q <= '9' && nd < 31) digits[nd++] = *q;
    q++;
}
if (*q == 'e' || *q == 'E') q++;
int exp10 = atoi(q);
while (nd > 1 && digits[nd - 1] == '0') nd--;

char out[96];
int k = 0;
if (sign) out[k++] = '-';
if (exp10 >= -4 && exp10 < 16) {
    if (exp10 >= 0) {
        int int_digits = exp10 + 1;
        if (nd <= int_digits) {
            for (int i = 0; i < nd; i++) out[k++] = digits[i];
            for (int i = nd; i < int_digits; i++) out[k++] = '0';
            out[k++] = '.';
            out[k++] = '0';
        } else {
            for (int i = 0; i < int_digits; i++) out[k++] = digits[i];
            out[k++] = '.';
            for (int i = int_digits; i < nd; i++) out[k++] = digits[i];
        }
    } else {
        out[k++] = '0';
        out[k++] = '.';
        for (int i = 0; i < -exp10 - 1; i++) out[k++] = '0';
        for (int i = 0; i < nd; i++) out[k++] = digits[i];
    }
} else {
    out[k++] = digits[0];
    if (nd > 1) {
        out[k++] = '.';
        for (int i = 1; i < nd; i++) out[k++] = digits[i];
    }
    out[k++] = 'e';
    if (exp10 < 0) { out[k++] = '-'; exp10 = -exp10; }
    else out[k++] = '+';
    char ebuf[16];
    snprintf(ebuf, sizeof ebuf, "%02d", exp10);
    for (const char *e = ebuf; *e; e++) out[k++] = *e;
}
out[k] = '\0';
return pengu_string_new(out);
"""

## Deep-copies a `JsonValue` with the derived `Imago` callback.
##
## ## Motivo
## A `derive Imago` helper is a C symbol; the public `clone` method needs to
## call it without exposing the helper name.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns a fully independent tree; release it with `banish`.
antiquus _json_clone_value with v as JsonValue into JsonValue:
    r"""
JsonValue out;
memset(&out, 0, sizeof out);
_pengu_clone_JsonValue(&out, &v);
return out;
"""

## Releases a `JsonValue` in place and zeroes it.
##
## ## Motivo
## `free` must work even when the caller has a `ref to JsonValue` (a method's
## `self`), where `banish` would release the pointer, not the payload.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees every owned buffer; the value becomes `Null`.
antiquus _json_free_raw with v as ref to JsonValue into void:
    r"""
if (!v) return;
_pengu_cleanup_JsonValue(v);
memset(v, 0, sizeof *v);
"""

## Copies a byte slice into a fresh owned string.
##
## ## Motivo
## `parse_bytes` / `validate_bytes` accept a `slice of byte`; the parser works
## on `string`, so one copy normalizes the representation.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates one owned buffer; release it with `banish`.
antiquus _json_bytes_to_string with s as slice of byte into string:
    r"""
int n = s.len;
char *buf = (char *)pengu_memoria_alloc((size_t)n + 1);
if (!buf) return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
if (n > 0 && s.data) memcpy(buf, s.data, (size_t)n);
buf[n] = '\0';
PenguString out;
out.data = buf;
out.len = n;
out.is_owned = 1;
return out;
"""

## Inserts or replaces `key -> value` in an object entry list, taking ownership
## of both.
##
## ## Motivo
## A weave parameter is an immutable binding, so the pure version could not
## `set entries at i` and could not update the header when `push` reallocates.
## The bridge mutates the caller's real `PenguList` header through a `ref`.
##
## ## Memoria
## On duplicate, frees the replaced value and the new key; on insert, the list
## takes ownership of both.
antiquus _json_obj_put with entries as ref to list of JsonEntry, key as string, value as JsonValue into void:
    r"""
PenguList *l = entries;
JsonEntry *es = (JsonEntry *)l->data;
for (int i = 0; i < l->len; i++) {
    if (pengu_string_equal(es[i].key, key)) {
        _pengu_cleanup_JsonValue(&es[i].value);
        es[i].value = value;
        pengu_banish_string(&key);
        return;
    }
}
JsonEntry e;
e.key = key;
e.value = value;
pengu_list_push(l, &e);
"""

## Releases only the box of a `result of JsonValue to JsonError`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `parse_in_arena` moves the value out of a successful result; the box must be
## freed without touching the payload, which now belongs to the caller.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees the payload slot, not the payload.
antiquus _json_drop_result_box with r as ref to result of JsonValue to JsonError into void:
    r"""
if (r->ok_val) { free(r->ok_val); r->ok_val = NULL; }
if (r->err_val) { free(r->err_val); r->err_val = NULL; }
"""

## Moves the payload out of a `maybe JsonValue` and frees only the box.
##
## ## Motivo
## A caller that wants to own the payload without a copy needs to consume the
## box; `banish` on the box would release the payload too.
##
## ## Memoria
## Transfers the payload to the caller and zeroes the box.
antiquus _json_take_value with m as ref to maybe JsonValue into JsonValue:
    r"""
if (m && m->is_present && m->value) {
    JsonValue out = *(JsonValue *)m->value;
    free(m->value);
    m->value = NULL;
    m->is_present = false;
    return out;
}
JsonValue empty;
memset(&empty, 0, sizeof empty);
return empty;
"""

## Moves the payload out of a `maybe string` and frees only the box.
##
## ## Motivo
## Same contract as `_json_take_value`, for the string accessors.
##
## ## Memoria
## Transfers the string to the caller and zeroes the box.
antiquus _json_take_string with m as ref to maybe string into string:
    r"""
if (m && m->is_present && m->value) {
    PenguString out = *(PenguString *)m->value;
    free(m->value);
    m->value = NULL;
    m->is_present = false;
    return out;
}
return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
"""

## Releases the box of a `maybe list of JsonValue` without its payload.
##
## ## Motivo
## `as_array` hands out an owned list; after `free_values` has released it the
## box must be freed without freeing the moved list again.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees the box allocation only.
antiquus _json_drop_maybe_values with m as ref to maybe list of JsonValue into void:
    r"""
if (m && m->value) { free(m->value); m->value = NULL; }
if (m) m->is_present = false;
"""

## Releases the box of a `maybe list of JsonEntry` without its payload.
##
## ## Motivo
## Same contract as `_json_drop_maybe_values`, for `as_object`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees the box allocation only.
antiquus _json_drop_maybe_entries with m as ref to maybe list of JsonEntry into void:
    r"""
if (m && m->value) { free(m->value); m->value = NULL; }
if (m) m->is_present = false;
"""

## Returns an owned copy of the byte range `[start, end)` of `s`.
##
## ## Motivo
## JSON Pointer tokenisation needs a substring without importing a full text
## module; the runtime helper already implements the exact ownership contract.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates one owned buffer; release it with `banish`.
antiquus _json_substring with s as string, start as int, end as int into string:
    r"""
return pengu_string_substring(s, start, end);
"""

## Reports whether `f` is finite.
##
## ## Motivo
## `stringify` must reject `NaN`/`Infinity` unless `allow_nan` is set, and
## `f != f` only detects NaN.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
antiquus _json_is_finite with f as f64 into bool:
    r"""
return isfinite(f) ? true : false;
"""

## Releases the *box* of a `maybe JsonValue` without releasing its payload.
##
## ## Motivo
## The `or:` form frees the box for you, but an `or:` block that does not
## mention `error` emits an unused variable in C. This helper lets internal
## code move the payload out and free only the box, keeping the generated C
## clean under `-Werror`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees the box allocation; the value it pointed at is left untouched.
antiquus _json_drop_maybe with m as ref to maybe JsonValue into void:
    r"""
if (m && m->value) { free(m->value); m->value = NULL; }
if (m) m->is_present = false;
"""

## Compares two strings byte-wise.
##
## ## Motivo
## `sort_keys` only needs the ordering; routing it through one C helper keeps
## the contract identical to `pengu_string_compare` used by derived `Ordo`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
antiquus _json_str_cmp with a as string, b as string into int:
    r"""
return pengu_string_compare(a, b);
"""

## Pushes `item` onto the array payload of `v`.
##
## ## Motivo
## A method on an algebraic omen cannot mutate `self`'s active union member
## through the language (the `judge` binding is a copy), so the few in-place
## mutators go through a two-line C bridge. The PenguScript wrapper checks the
## tag and panics with a useful message first.
##
## ## Memoria
## The list owns the copied element; `item`'s buffers are not duplicated, so
## ownership of the payload transfers to the array.
antiquus _json_push_arr with v as ref to JsonValue, item as JsonValue into void:
    r"""
if (v && v->tag == JsonValue_Arr) {
    pengu_list_push(&v->data.Arr.items, &item);
}
"""

## Moves the last array element into `out` and shrinks the array.
##
## ## Motivo
## `pop` transfers ownership without copying; doing it from PenguScript would
## require reading an element after decrementing the length.
##
## ## Memoria
## `out` receives the element bytes; the array no longer references them.
antiquus _json_pop_arr with v as ref to JsonValue, out as ref to JsonValue into bool:
    r"""
if (!v || v->tag != JsonValue_Arr || v->data.Arr.items.len <= 0) return false;
PenguList *l = &v->data.Arr.items;
l->len--;
*out = ((JsonValue *)l->data)[l->len];
return true;
"""

## Replaces array element `idx`, releasing the old payload.
##
## ## Motivo
## Replacing an element must release the subtree it held; that is the derived
## destructor, which is only reachable from C.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees the old element, stores `item` (ownership transfers).
antiquus _json_set_at_arr with v as ref to JsonValue, idx as int, item as JsonValue into bool:
    r"""
if (!v || v->tag != JsonValue_Arr) return false;
PenguList *l = &v->data.Arr.items;
if (idx < 0 || idx >= l->len) return false;
JsonValue *slot = &((JsonValue *)l->data)[idx];
_pengu_cleanup_JsonValue(slot);
*slot = item;
return true;
"""

## Inserts or replaces `key -> item` in an object, copying the key.
##
## ## Motivo
## The object stores owned keys, and replacing an existing value must release
## the old subtree.
##
## ## Memoria
## Copies `key`; takes ownership of `item`; frees a replaced value.
antiquus _json_set_key_obj with v as ref to JsonValue, key as string, item as JsonValue into void:
    r"""
if (!v || v->tag != JsonValue_Obj) return;
PenguList *l = &v->data.Obj.entries;
JsonEntry *es = (JsonEntry *)l->data;
for (int i = 0; i < l->len; i++) {
    if (pengu_string_equal(es[i].key, key)) {
        _pengu_cleanup_JsonValue(&es[i].value);
        es[i].value = item;
        return;
    }
}
JsonEntry e;
e.key = pengu_string_copy(key);
e.value = item;
pengu_list_push(l, &e);
"""

## Removes `key` from an object, moving its value into `out`.
##
## ## Motivo
## Removal must free the object's key and shift the remaining entries.
##
## ## Memoria
## Frees the stored key; `out` receives the value; the entry is removed.
antiquus _json_remove_key_obj with v as ref to JsonValue, key as string, out as ref to JsonValue into bool:
    r"""
if (!v || v->tag != JsonValue_Obj) return false;
PenguList *l = &v->data.Obj.entries;
JsonEntry *es = (JsonEntry *)l->data;
for (int i = 0; i < l->len; i++) {
    if (pengu_string_equal(es[i].key, key)) {
        *out = es[i].value;
        pengu_banish_string(&es[i].key);
        if (i + 1 < l->len) {
            memmove(&es[i], &es[i + 1], (size_t)(l->len - i - 1) * sizeof(JsonEntry));
        }
        l->len--;
        return true;
    }
}
return false;
"""

## Returns a non-owning `string` view over `[p, p + n)` in arena memory.
##
## ## Motivo
## `parse_in_arena` must not allocate string bytes on the heap; a header with
## `is_owned == 0` makes `banish` a no-op.
##
## ## Memoria
## Borrows the arena block. Valid until the arena is reset or freed.
antiquus _json_arena_string with p as ref to byte, n as int into string:
    r"""
PenguString s;
s.data = (char *)p;
s.len = n;
s.is_owned = 0;
return s;
"""

## Builds a non-owning `list of JsonValue` header over arena memory.
##
## ## Motivo
## The arena owns the element buffer. `cap = -1` marks the header as
## non-owning: `banish` does not `free` an arena pointer and `push` refuses to
## grow it.
##
## ## Memoria
## Borrows the arena block; valid until the arena is reset or freed.
antiquus _json_arena_list with p as ref to JsonValue, n as int into list of JsonValue:
    r"""
PenguList l;
l.data = p;
l.len = n;
l.cap = -1;
l.elem_size = sizeof(JsonValue);
return l;
"""

## Builds a non-owning `list of JsonEntry` header over arena memory.
##
## ## Motivo
## Same contract as `_json_arena_list`, for object entries.
##
## ## Memoria
## Borrows the arena block; valid until the arena is reset or freed.
antiquus _json_arena_entries with p as ref to JsonEntry, n as int into list of JsonEntry:
    r"""
PenguList l;
l.data = p;
l.len = n;
l.cap = -1;
l.elem_size = sizeof(JsonEntry);
return l;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Small pure helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Returns the `i64` value `9223372036854775807`.
##
## ## Retorno
## `i64` max, useful when clamping.
weave i64_max into i64:
    return 9223372036854775807

## Returns the `i64` value `-9223372036854775808`.
##
## ## Retorno
## `i64` min. Written as `(-max) - 1` because the positive literal does not fit.
weave i64_min into i64:
    return (0 - 9223372036854775807) - 1

## Appends one Unicode codepoint to a builder as UTF-8.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sb`: destination builder. Mutated.
## - `cp`: a scalar value in `[0, 0x10FFFF]`, excluding the surrogate range.
##
## ## Retorno
## Nothing.
##
## ## Memoria
## Appends into the builder's buffer; no temporary string is allocated.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling json._append_codepoint with (sigil of sb), 0x1F600
## ```
weave _append_codepoint with sb as ref to StringBuilder, cp as int into void:
    var buf as array of byte with size 4 is [0, 0, 0, 0]
    if cp < 128:
        set buf at 0 is (cp to byte)
        calling sb->append_bytes with (buf at 0 to 1)
        return
    if cp < 2048:
        set buf at 0 is (192 + (cp >> 6)) to byte
        set buf at 1 is (128 + (cp & 63)) to byte
        calling sb->append_bytes with (buf at 0 to 2)
        return
    if cp < 65536:
        set buf at 0 is (224 + (cp >> 12)) to byte
        set buf at 1 is (128 + ((cp >> 6) & 63)) to byte
        set buf at 2 is (128 + (cp & 63)) to byte
        calling sb->append_bytes with (buf at 0 to 3)
        return
    set buf at 0 is (240 + (cp >> 18)) to byte
    set buf at 1 is (128 + ((cp >> 12) & 63)) to byte
    set buf at 2 is (128 + ((cp >> 6) & 63)) to byte
    set buf at 3 is (128 + (cp & 63)) to byte
    calling sb->append_bytes with (buf at 0 to 4)

## Returns the value of one hexadecimal digit byte, or `-1`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `b`: an ASCII byte value.
##
## ## Retorno
## `0..15` for `0-9`, `a-f`, `A-F`; `-1` otherwise.
weave _hex_val with b as int into int:
    if b >= 48 and b <= 57:
        return b - 48
    if b >= 97 and b <= 102:
        return b - 87
    if b >= 65 and b <= 70:
        return b - 55
    return -1

## Returns the byte value of a lowercase hex digit.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `v`: `0..15`.
##
## ## Retorno
## The ASCII byte for `0123456789abcdef`; `48` for an out-of-range value.
weave _hex_byte with v as int into byte:
    if v < 10:
        return (48 + v) to byte
    return (87 + v) to byte

## Appends a `\uXXXX` escape for the low 16 bits of `cp`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `sb`: destination builder. Mutated.
## - `cp`: a UTF-16 code unit.
##
## ## Retorno
## Nothing.
weave _append_u4 with sb as ref to StringBuilder, cp as int into void:
    calling sb->append with "\\u"
    var h0 as int is calling _hex_byte with ((cp >> 12) & 15)
    var h1 as int is calling _hex_byte with ((cp >> 8) & 15)
    var h2 as int is calling _hex_byte with ((cp >> 4) & 15)
    var h3 as int is calling _hex_byte with (cp & 15)
    calling sb->append_char with (h0 to char)
    calling sb->append_char with (h1 to char)
    calling sb->append_char with (h2 to char)
    calling sb->append_char with (h3 to char)

## Frees every element of a `list of JsonValue`, then the list itself.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `items`: an owned list (for example the result of `as_array`, `values`,
##   `find_key` or `parse_in_arena` is **not** owned; do not free that one).
##
## ## Retorno
## Nothing.
##
## ## Memoria
## Banishes each value recursively, then the list buffer.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var items as list of JsonValue is (calling root.as_array) or else json.empty_values
## calling json.free_values with items
## ```
weave free_values with items as list of JsonValue into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < items.len:
        var v as JsonValue is items at i
        banish v
        set i is i + 1
    banish items

## Frees every entry of a `list of JsonEntry`, then the list itself.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `entries`: an owned list, such as the result of `as_object` or `entries`.
##
## ## Retorno
## Nothing.
##
## ## Memoria
## Banishes each entry (its key and value), then the list buffer.
weave free_entries with entries as list of JsonEntry into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < entries.len:
        var e as JsonEntry is entries at i
        banish e
        set i is i + 1
    banish entries

## Frees every string of a `list of string`, then the list itself.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `items`: an owned list of strings, such as the result of `keys`.
##
## ## Retorno
## Nothing.
##
## ## Memoria
## Banishes each string copy, then the list buffer.
weave free_strings with items as list of string into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < items.len:
        var s as string is items at i
        banish s
        set i is i + 1
    banish items

## Moves the value out of a `maybe JsonValue`, freeing only the box.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional. The box is consumed; do not use it afterwards.
##
## ## Retorno
## The payload (owned; release it with `banish`), or `JsonValue.Null` when the
## optional was absent.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var opt as maybe JsonValue is calling root.get with "key"
## var value as JsonValue is calling json.take_value with (sigil of opt)
## defer banish value
## ```
weave take_value with m as ref to maybe JsonValue into JsonValue:
    return calling _json_take_value with m

## Moves the string out of a `maybe string`, freeing only the box.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional. The box is consumed; do not use it afterwards.
##
## ## Retorno
## The string (owned; release it with `banish`), or `""` when absent.
weave take_string with m as ref to maybe string into string:
    return calling _json_take_string with m

## Member `key` as an owned deep copy, or `JsonValue.Null` when absent.
##
## This is the box-free variant of `get`, for code that wants a plain value
## without a `maybe` wrapper.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `v`: an object (other kinds return `Null`). Borrowed.
## - `key`: the member name. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `JsonValue`; release it with `banish`.
weave get_or_null with v as JsonValue, key as string into JsonValue:
    var out as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.null_value
    var ignored as int is judge v:
        when Obj with entries ->
            for e in entries:
                if e.key == key:
                    set out is calling _json_clone_value with e.value
            0
        else ->
            0
    return out

## Element `i` as an owned deep copy, or `JsonValue.Null` when out of range.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `v`: an array (other kinds return `Null`). Borrowed.
## - `i`: the 0-based index.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `JsonValue`; release it with `banish`.
weave at_or_null with v as JsonValue, i as int into JsonValue:
    var out as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.null_value
    var ignored as int is judge v:
        when Arr with items ->
            if i >= 0 and i < items.len:
                set out is calling _json_clone_value with (items at i)
            0
        else ->
            0
    return out

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Constructors
#
# `ritual`s of the `JsonValue` omen. `JsonValue.null_value` and friends are the
# canonical spelling; the module-level aliases below are handy inside this
# module and for callers that already imported `json as j`.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting JsonValue:
    ## Constructs the JSON `null`.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Null`.
    weave ritual null_value into JsonValue:
        return with Null is 0

    ## Constructs a boolean value.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `b`: the boolean. Copied.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Bool`.
    weave ritual bool_val with b as bool into JsonValue:
        return with Bool is b

    ## Constructs an integer value.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `i`: an `i64`. Copied.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Int`.
    weave ritual int_val with i as i64 into JsonValue:
        return with Int is i

    ## Constructs a floating-point value.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `f`: an `f64`. Copied.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Float`.
    weave ritual float_val with f as f64 into JsonValue:
        return with Float is f

    ## Constructs a string value, taking ownership of `s`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `s`: the text. The returned value owns the buffer; do not banish `s`
    ##   after the call.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Str`.
    weave ritual string_val with s as string into JsonValue:
        return with Str is s

    ## Constructs an empty array.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Arr` with a fresh empty list.
    weave ritual empty_array into JsonValue:
        return with Arr is list of JsonValue

    ## Constructs an empty object.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `JsonValue.Obj` with a fresh empty entry list.
    weave ritual empty_object into JsonValue:
        return with Obj is list of JsonEntry

